    {
      "id": "mjyrjuq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Mineral Resources"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Minerals in India are broadly categorized into Metallic (Ferrous/Non-Ferrous), Non-Metallic, and Energy Resources.",
        "The North-Eastern Peninsular Belt, encompassing the Chota Nagpur Plateau, is India's richest mineral region.",
        "Gondwana coalfields constitute over 98% of India's total coal reserves, concentrated mainly in river valleys like Damodar and Mahanadi.",
        "Petroleum resources are primarily concentrated in offshore fields like Bombay High and onshore regions like Assam and Gujarat.",
        "Conservation strategies, including efficient extraction, recycling, and renewable alternatives, are vital for managing non-renewable mineral reserves."
      ],
      "id": "723xgxt"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vcjwdr7",
      "content": "• Minerals are natural substances found in rocks."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "065ti8c",
      "content": "• They are formed through geological processes over millions of years."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p5q6m20",
      "content": "• Minerals are essential raw materials for industries."
    },
